3.4 The Contractor shall submit an application for payment (an "Interim Payment Application") to the Employer's Agent not later than the twenty-fifth (25th) day of each calendar month. Each Interim Payment Application shall set out:

(a) the estimated Contract Sum value of the Works executed up to and including the preceding day, calculated in accordance with Clause 3.5;

(b) the value of any materials or goods on Site which have been delivered to the Site for incorporation in the Works and which are vested in the Employer pursuant to Clause 18;

(c) the value of any materials or goods off Site which have been paid for by the Contractor and which are vested in the Employer pursuant to Clause 18, together with such evidence of vesting as the Employer's Agent may reasonably require;

(d) the amount of any loss and/or expense to which the Contractor considers itself entitled pursuant to Clause 14 (Compensation Events);

(e) the amount of any variation instruction issued pursuant to Clause 7 (Variations) for which the Contractor has not previously applied for payment;

(f) the amount of any other sum which the Contractor considers to be due to it under this Contract; and

(g) the amounts to be deducted pursuant to Clause 3.6.

3.5 The value of the Works executed shall be assessed by the Employer's Agent in accordance with the following principles:

(a) the measured works shall be valued in accordance with the rates and prices set out in the Contract Documents, or, where no rate or price is applicable, at a fair and reasonable rate or price;

(b) the value of works executed shall include the value of materials or goods which have been delivered to the Site for incorporation in the Works and which are not prematurely, negligently or wilfully damaged or removed;

(c) the value of any variations shall be assessed in accordance with Clause 7; and

(d) the value of any works which are defective or do not comply with this Contract shall be excluded from the assessment until such time as the defects have been remedied to the reasonable satisfaction of the Employer's Agent.

3.6 The Employer's Agent shall, within ten (10) days of receipt of each Interim Payment Application, issue an Interim Payment Certificate certifying the amount due to the Contractor (or, as the case may be, the amount due from the Contractor to the Employer), which shall be the net of:

