(a) the amounts referred to in Clause 3.4(a) to (f) inclusive; less

(b) the following deductions:

(i) retention money in accordance with Clause 3.7;

(ii) amounts previously certified and paid;

(iii) any amounts which the Employer is entitled to deduct or set off pursuant to this Contract, including any sums due under Clause 16 (Defects Liability) or Clause 19 (Termination); and

(iv) any amount in respect of VAT which the Employer is entitled to deduct in accordance with applicable law.

3.7 **Retention**

3.7.1 The Employer shall retain from each Interim Payment Certificate an amount equal to five per cent (5%) of the amount otherwise due to the Contractor under Clause 3.6(a), up to a maximum aggregate retention of **£925,000 (nine hundred and twenty-five thousand pounds sterling)** (the "Retention Fund").

3.7.2 The Retention Fund shall be released to the Contractor as follows:

(a) one half of the Retention Fund shall be released and paid to the Contractor upon the issue of the Certificate of Practical Completion pursuant to Clause 5.4; and

(b) the balance of the Retention Fund shall be released and paid to the Contractor upon the issue of the Certificate of Making Good Defects pursuant to Clause 16.3.

3.7.3 The Employer may, at its sole discretion, accept a Parent Company Guarantee or other approved security in lieu of retention in accordance with the provisions of Clause 21.

3.8 **Payment Schedule**

2.2.1 The following sub-contractors are named in respect of the works described in the Employer's Requirements and the Contractor's Proposals, and the Contractor shall enter into sub-contracts with each such named sub-contractor on terms no less favourable to the Employer than the terms set out in the relevant sub-contract particulars:

| Ref | Named Sub-Contractor | Scope of Works | Sub-Contract Value (GBP) |
|-----|----------------------|----------------|--------------------------|
| NS-01 | Meridian Electrical & Mechanical Services Limited | Design, supply, installation, testing and commissioning of all mechanical and electrical building services including HVAC, public health, power, lighting, fire alarm, and building management system (BMS) as more particularly described in the M&E Scope at Annex A to these Particulars | £4,200,000 |

2.2.2 The sub-contract value stated at NS-01 above is the agreed contract sum for the M&E sub-contract (Contract B-2023-027) and is current as at the date of this Contract. For the avoidance of doubt, the sub-contract value of £4,200,000 (four million two hundred thousand pounds sterling) shall be the maximum amount payable to the named sub-contractor in respect of the M&E Works, subject only to authorised variations in accordance with Clause 6 (Variations) of this Contract.

2.2.3 The M&E Works comprise the design, supply, installation, testing and commissioning of:

(a) all mechanical services including heating, ventilation, air conditioning, chilled water generation and distribution, domestic hot and cold water services, above-ground drainage and natural gas installations;

(b) all electrical services including LV distribution, power and lighting installations, small power, containment, earthing and bonding, and lightning protection;

(c) fire detection and alarm systems, emergency lighting, and fire-fighting installations including sprinkler and dry riser systems;

(d) the building management system (BMS) including all control panels, sensors, actuators, outstations and the central monitoring workstation;

(e) vertical transportation comprising two (2) passenger lifts and one (1) goods lift, including all lift shaft steelwork, guide rails, doors, cars, counterweights, machines and controls;

(f) all associated builders' work in connection with the M&E installations including cutting, chasing, drilling, forming openings, fire stopping and penetration sealing; and

(g) testing, commissioning, balancing, demonstration and training, together with the provision of operation and maintenance manuals and as-built records.

2.2.4 The M&E Works shall be carried out in accordance with the M&E Scope, the Employer's Requirements and the Contractor's Proposals, and shall achieve the performance criteria set out in the Performance Specification at Annex B to these Particulars.

